-- title:
--   Scaling injective centre families apart
-- statement:
--   Let $a_i$ and $b_i$, for $i$ in a finite set, be two injective families of points in $\mathbb R^3$, and let $D\ge0$ and $R\in\mathbb R$. Then there is $\Lambda$ with $\Lambda\ge1$ and $\Lambda\ge R+2$ such that both scaled families are $D$-separated:
--   $$
--   \forall\,i\ne j\ \ \exists\,k:\ |\Lambda a_{ik}-\Lambda a_{jk}|>D,\qquad\text{and likewise for }b .
--   $$
--
--   Expanding the source and target layouts this way makes room to rearrange boxes freely.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/MathematicalPhysics/NavierStokes/BalancedTransport/Routing.lean#L77-L102

